            <li class="toc__item toc__item--l2"><a href="#pre-order-bonuses">Pre-order bonuses</a></li>
            <li class="toc__item toc__item--l2"><a href="#how-to-buy">How to buy</a></li>
            <li class="toc__item toc__item--l2"><a href="#good-to-know">Good to know</a></li>
            <li class="toc__item toc__item--l2"><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
          </ol>
        </details>
      </aside>

      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> <strong>Standard $79.99 / £69.99 / €79.99.</strong> <strong>Ultimate $99.99 / £89.99 / €99.99.</strong> Both are for PS5 and Xbox Series X|S only.</li>
<li><strong>Ultimate = the game + $20 / £20 of extra items</strong> (cars, guns, clothes, shops). It is not early access. You can add it later with the Ultimate Edition Upgrade ($20 on Xbox).</li>
<li><strong>Buy before 20 Nov 2026</strong> to get the Vintage Vice City Pack. <strong>Digital buyers also get 1 month of GTA+</strong> (it renews at the normal price until you cancel).</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>Edition</em> is a version of the game you can buy. <em>Digital</em> means you download it. <em>Code-in-box</em> means a box with a download code inside and <strong>no disc</strong>. <em>GTA+</em> is Rockstar’s paid club, with a monthly fee.</p>
<h2 id="prices" tabindex="-1">Prices</h2>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Edition</th>
<th>USD</th>
<th>GBP</th>
<th>EUR</th>
<th>How you get it</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Standard</td>
<td>$79.99</td>
<td>£69.99</td>
<td>€79.99</td>
<td>Digital, or code-in-box</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Ultimate</td>
<td>$99.99</td>
<td>£89.99</td>
<td>€99.99</td>
<td>Digital only</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Ultimate Edition Upgrade</td>
<td>$20.00 (Xbox Store)</td>
<td>£20.00 (Xbox Store, per a price tracker)</td>
<td>not confirmed</td>
<td>Add-on. Needs the game first.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<ul>
<li><strong>USD:</strong> Rockstar’s press release (24 June 2026) and the PlayStation and Xbox US stores.</li>
<li><strong>GBP:</strong> £69.99 is on the UK PlayStation Store. £89.99 and the £20 upgrade come from price trackers that read the UK stores (Six Star Ledger, checked 16 Nov), and from PC Gamer’s pre-order guide.</li>
<li><strong>EUR:</strong> €79.99 and €99.99 on the Italian and Portuguese PlayStation Stores, and other euro stores are reported to match. Countries outside the euro have other prices, not listed here.</li>
<li><strong>PS5 upgrade price:</strong> not announced. The PlayStation listing showed no separate price.</li>
<li>US and Canada prices are usually shown before sales tax. UK and euro prices include VAT.</li>
</ul>
<p>![price comparison table graphic for Standard and Ultimate](TODO: image:editions-prices-step-1 — diagram, our own art: two cards, Standard and Ultimate, with USD, GBP and EUR prices)
<em>Caption: Diagram. Standard and Ultimate side by side.</em></p>
<h2 id="what-is-in-the-ultimate-edition" tabindex="-1">What is in the Ultimate Edition</h2>
<p>The Ultimate Edition adds the <strong>Ultimate Edition Upgrade</strong>. The PlayStation and Xbox store pages name these items:</p>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Group</th>
<th>Items</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Cars, boat, bike</td>
<td>'95 Grotti Cheetah, Dinka Enduro motorcycle (army colours), Crest Kayak, Shitzu Squalo boat, '67 Vapid Dominator Buggy with the Paradise Garage in Watson Bay</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Guns</td>
<td>Hawk and Little Morgan revolvers, engraved versions of the Girardi ES9 and Klose K17 pistols</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Clothes and looks</td>
<td>Vice City Style outfits, hairstyles and tattoos; Goodtime Gear (Macca the Gator clothes)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Extras</td>
<td>Ganado Retro Build (mods for Jason’s pickup), Classic Car Collection, PTT Youngin$ Compound</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shops only open with Ultimate</td>
<td>Rideout Customs, Sara’s Unisex Salon, Stock 305, Electric Fang Tattoo (50+ tattoos), One-Eyed Willie’s</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Rockstar says the items are spread across the story, “with new items uncovered behind each chapter”. So you do <strong>not</strong> get all of it at the start.</p>
<h2 id="pre-order-bonuses" tabindex="-1">Pre-order bonuses</h2>
<p><strong>Vintage Vice City Pack</strong> (both editions). Buy or pre-order <strong>before 20 November 2026</strong>. Per Polygon and The Verge it includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>a '55 Vapid Stanier car</li>
<li>a garage near Ocean Beach with a weapon locker and a place to drop off stolen goods</li>
<li>outfits and hairstyles</li>
<li>a tropical pattern for weapons</li>
</ul>
<p>The PlayStation Store text in some regions says “by November 19”, so buy before 19 Nov if you can.</p>
<p><strong>1 month of GTA+, free, for digital buyers</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>PS5:</strong> buy on PlayStation Store, then open the <strong>GTA+</strong> page on the Store and follow the steps. <strong>Claim it by 31 March 2027.</strong> One claim per account. The Ultimate Edition Upgrade bought alone does not count.</li>
<li><strong>Xbox:</strong> open the Store, select your <strong>profile icon</strong> at the top left, then select <strong>Offers &amp; credits</strong>, and claim it there (Microsoft Store text).</li>
<li>After one month it renews monthly at the normal price. Cancel before the next payment date if you do not want it.</li>
<li>Boxed copies get the Vintage Vice City Pack, but the free GTA+ month is for <strong>digital</strong> buyers.</li>
</ul>
<p>![PS5 Store page for GTA VI with edition choices](TODO: image:editions-prices-step-2 — step screenshot, PS5: PlayStation Store GTA VI page showing Standard and Ultimate)
<em>Caption: Step screenshot. Choose your edition on the PlayStation Store.</em></p>
<p>![Xbox Offers and credits screen with the GTA+ offer](TODO: image:editions-prices-step-3 — menu screen, Xbox: Store profile icon &gt; Offers &amp; credits with the GTA+ month offer)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. Where to claim the free GTA+ month on Xbox.</em></p>
<h2 id="how-to-buy" tabindex="-1">How to buy</h2>
<p><strong>PS5:</strong> open <strong>PlayStation Store</strong>, search <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>, choose <strong>Standard</strong> or <strong>Ultimate</strong>, then select the buy or pre-order button.</p>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S:</strong> open the <strong>Microsoft Store</strong>, search <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>, choose <strong>Standard</strong> or <strong>Ultimate</strong>, then select <strong>Buy</strong> or <strong>Pre-order</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>Boxed (Standard only):</strong> buy at the Rockstar Store or a shop, open the box, then enter the code on your console store. There is no disc. Codes from the PlayStation Store can be tied to your country, so use the right one.</p>
<p><strong>Standard now, Ultimate later?</strong> Yes. Buy the Ultimate Edition Upgrade. On Xbox the upgrade costs the same as the price gap ($20), so you pay the same in total.</p>
<h2 id="good-to-know" tabindex="-1">Good to know</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>No microtransactions at launch:</strong> Rockstar told Kinda Funny this (per GameSpot). The store pages still show “In-game purchases optional”. Treat the first as a statement from an interview.</li>
<li><strong>Collector’s merch:</strong> a $399.99 Rockstar Store box (merch only, the game is sold separately), per Technobezz. Not a game edition.</li>
<li><strong>Not announced:</strong> PS5 upgrade price, euro prices outside the euro area, season passes or paid add-ons.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="how-much-does-gta-6-cost" tabindex="-1">How much does GTA 6 cost?</h3>
<p>Standard: $79.99, £69.99, €79.99. Ultimate: $99.99, £89.99, €99.99.</p>
<h3 id="is-there-a-disc" tabindex="-1">Is there a disc?</h3>
<p>No. The boxed version has a download code and no disc.</p>
<h3 id="what-do-i-get-with-the-ultimate-edition" tabindex="-1">What do I get with the Ultimate Edition?</h3>
<p>The game plus extra cars, guns, clothes and shops. They unlock across the story.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-upgrade-from-standard-to-ultimate" tabindex="-1">Can I upgrade from Standard to Ultimate?</h3>
<p>Yes. The Ultimate Edition Upgrade is $20 on Xbox. The PS5 price is not announced.</p>
<h3 id="what-is-the-vintage-vice-city-pack" tabindex="-1">What is the Vintage Vice City Pack?</h3>
<p>A bonus for buying before 20 November 2026. See the list above.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-claim-the-free-gta-month" tabindex="-1">How do I claim the free GTA+ month?</h3>
<p>PS5: use the GTA+ page on PlayStation Store, before 31 March 2027. Xbox: profile icon &gt; Offers &amp; credits.</p>
